SUMMARY:How Pleasant to Know Mr. Lear
DESCRIPTION:Dennis Duffy discusses the genius of Edward Lear as a painter and poet\, the great joiner of oil painting and printed nonsense. \nLear was a singular eccentric in his bespoke but loosely-fitting suits and his runcible hat\, he created work placing him among the finest of graphic cartoonists and satirists. This presentation explores that jagged world that he made up for himself\, in order to preserve his own complex selfhood. \n​Presented by Dennis Duffy\, Professor Emeritus\, Department of English\, University of Toronto. \nRegistration is recommended. Register online at https://tpl.ca/locations/DA/\, in person at the branch\, or by calling 416-393-7783.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/how-pleasant-to-know-mr-lear/
LOCATION:Danforth Coxwell Library\, 1675 Danforth Avenue\, Toronto\, M4C 5P2
ORGANIZER;CN="Danforth Coxwell Branch%2C Toronto Public Library":MAILTO:dastaff@tpl.ca
END:VEVENT
